From: EglantinePS5
Subject: up: the split front skips the instance-loop writes the back ignores (EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP), off by default

What: with the GPU thread split and macros on the front (EDEN_NX2_SPLIT=2), the front no longer
sends draw.end inside an instance loop (DrawEnd draws nothing in DrawMode::Instance) and
vertex_buffer.first / vertex_buffer.count writes that keep their value (instance loop methods: they
flush no deferred draw, and the draw manager only reads them at the draw). Each was a ring entry
and a CallMethod on the back, the busy thread when walking. index_buffer writes are always sent
(they mark the index buffer dirty). The front tracks the back's loop from draw.begin (instance id
First leaves a loop, Subsequent enters one) and the inline index methods, for every word of a
multi-method write and with the value the back acts on in Replay mode.
#488's fix is in: the front tracks whether the back's method sink holds state writes (a plain
Method entry of a state register leaves one there; a Regs or CbData block, a direct macro write, an
executable method and a multi-method run consume it) and skips nothing while it does, since a
changed write there ends a deferred draw that must issue before the next engine's work. #488's
second half (a front copied in an earlier split start) is taken as a check, not a re-copy: our
split stops only at shutdown, and a copy whose GpuSplit::SessionGeneration() differs skips nothing.
Ours on top: a macro sent to the back (EDEN_UP_L1056_BACK_MACROS) resets the loop to "not in one"
and the sink to "may hold writes", so a draw.end is sent until the next loop begins.
Old port 0352 (lichii-gpu-0214, EDEN_NX2_LOOP_SKIP, left out at the v1.219.020 move) not revived:
it tracked only the last word of a multi-method write (the bug upstream fixed in #178's last
commit) and had no #488. Ported fresh from upstream.

Switches (read once, when the split front is made): EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP=1 (exact "1"), only with
the same-value skip on (EDEN_NX2_SKIP_SAME and EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_SKIP not 0); unset or anything else
off. Off: no tracking, no counting; the same entries are sent as before. EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_VERIFY=1
still works with it on (a skip leaves the registers equal: it finds a wrong value, not a lost draw).
Log (HW_GPU): at start "EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP=1: the split front does not send ..." (Info), or
"EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP=1 does nothing: ..." (Warning); at the first skip and then every 4 Mi skipped
writes "EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP: N writes not sent (E draw.end in an instance loop, V
vertex_buffer.first/count), K same-value ones sent because the back's sink held state writes; R a
second since the last line". With EDEN_NX2_GPU_PROFILE the skips also count as SameValueWrites.

Origin and credit: zortos293/Lichii 7e2a9fe20c (#178), Thibaut LÉAUX, and its fix 5ba52f7720
(#488), Marc Stampfli. Upstream: Ocarina of Time, the village, 28.8 -> 30.6 fps on a PC with 0
EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_VERIFY differences; ~520,000 draw.end and ~390,000 same-value vertex_buffer.count
writes a second there. The console's rates are not known (the log line gives them).
